Sigh,
 
Having faithfully followed all sorts of great advice from this group
and the spoilers file, I finally got to the point where I could 
tackle the wiz fairly well.  
 
So there I was, on level 45 of hell.  I had just beaten the tar
out of the wizard with my +8 Mjollnir, had a miserable armor class
(only -5) but had speed boots and loads of fun intrinsics so I
wasn't too worried.  I even had that nice potion of paralysis and
loads of food so I thought I would pull that stunt to make the
outward bound trip better.  A wonderful rust monster stumbled
into me so I slew him with one mighty blow from Mjollnir and ate
him (no use wasting food, eh?).  I then get the message:  you feel
sick.  No sweat, I have my trusty unicorn horn along, so, I'll just
apply that (since I was lawful and thus couldn't pray).  
 
This was a majorly bad move.  It seems the wonderful wiz had cursed
my horn whilst I was not looking and the epitaph reads:
 
Grover 234HP ]254 max( poisoned by a unicorn horn (with the amulet).
 
Sigh . . .
 
